# No git push by default

- Do **not** run `git push` (or any remote publish of commits) unless the user explicitly asks to push or deploy in that message.
- Commits are still only when the user asks to commit (existing rule).
- "Ship it", "make it live", or similar does **not** authorize a push by itself — ask first or wait for an explicit push/deploy request.
